nodes:
- _type: Monitor
  name: AI HTTP Probe Unsuccessful
  identifier: urn:stackpack:suse-ai:monitor:http-probe-unavailable
  description: An explicitly configured endpoint check does not return HTTP 2xx. This is probe health, not application
    request error rate.
  intervalSeconds: 60
  status: ENABLED
  function: urn:stackpack:common:monitor-function:threshold
  arguments:
    threshold: 1
    comparator: LT
    failureState: DEVIATING
    metric:
      aliasTemplate: HTTP probe success
      unit: short
      query: min by (service_namespace, service_name) (httpcheck_status{suse_ai_observation_kind="http-probe", service_namespace!="",
        service_name!="", http_status_class="2xx"} and topk by (k8s_cluster_name, service_namespace, service_name,
        service_instance_id, http_url) (1, timestamp(httpcheck_status{suse_ai_observation_kind="http-probe", service_namespace!="",
        service_name!="", http_status_class="2xx"})))
    titleTemplate: An observed HTTP endpoint check failed
    urnTemplate: urn:opentelemetry:namespace/${service_namespace}:service/${service_name}
  remediationHint: Check the configured endpoint, authentication and pod readiness. Probe duration is not model
    inference latency. This monitor requires observed probe telemetry; a never-observed service cannot produce a
    result.
